                  "The court decides to do substantial justice under the substantive law, not bound by rules of practice, pleading or evidence except privilege and the dead-man rule. An itemized bill or invoice, receipted or marked paid, or two itemized estimates for services or repairs, are admissible and prima facie evidence of the reasonable value and necessity of the work; the owner still bears the burden on amounts kept from the deposit (NY:GOL-7-108(1-a)(f)). Disclosure only by court order.",
