                  "The court directs judgment on its findings and may condition its entry on just terms; before judgment it may order the tenant examined and restrained as if a post-judgment restraining notice had been served. It may transfer the claim to another part. The tenant's counterclaim (for example for the deposit or double damages) is allowed only within the part's monetary limit ($10,000); a larger claim is brought in a court of competent jurisdiction.",
